### Description
This Terraform program creates two Elastic Beanstalk environments that share the same Elastic Beanstalk application. It also sets up an IAM role named `eb_ec2_role` and an instance profile named `eb_ec2_profile`. The Elastic Beanstalk application uses the IAM role for its service role.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "eb_ec2_role" {
  name = "eb_ec2_role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_instance_profile" "eb_ec2_profile" {
  name = "eb_ec2_profile"
  role = aws_iam_role.eb_ec2_role.name
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_application" "my_application" {
  name = "my_application"

  appversion_lifecycle {
    service_role = aws_iam_role.eb_ec2_role.arn
    max_count    = 128
    delete_source_from_s3 = true
  }
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment" "environment1" {
  name                = "environment1"
  application         = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.my_application.name
  solution_stack_name = "64bit Amazon Linux 2 v3.6.0 running Python 3.9"
  instance_profile    = aws_iam_instance_profile.eb_ec2_profile.name
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment" "environment2" {
  name                = "environment2"
  application         = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.my_application.name
  solution_stack_name = "64bit Amazon Linux 2 v3.6.0 running Python 3.9"
  instance_profile    = aws_iam_instance_profile.eb_ec2_profile.name
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **IAM Role (`aws_iam_role`)**: An IAM role named `eb_ec2_role` is created with an assume role policy that allows EC2 to assume the role.
3. **IAM Instance Profile (`aws_iam_instance_profile`)**: An instance profile named `eb_ec2_profile` is created and linked to the `eb_ec2_role`.
4. **Elastic Beanstalk Application (`aws_elastic_beanstalk_application`)**: An Elastic Beanstalk application named `my_application` is created. It includes an `appversion_lifecycle` block that specifies the service role and lifecycle settings.
5. **Elastic Beanstalk Environments (`aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment`)**: Two environments, `environment1` and `environment2`, are created using the same Elastic Beanstalk application. Each environment uses the `eb_ec2_profile` instance profile and a specified solution stack.

