### Description

This Terraform program configures a Blue/Green deployment using AWS Elastic Beanstalk environments and AWS Route53 for traffic management. It includes two Elastic Beanstalk environments named "blue" and "green", and a Route53 hosted zone with weighted routing records to distribute traffic between these environments. The program ensures that the resources are properly created and interconnected based on their dependencies.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "application_name" {
  description = "Name of the Elastic Beanstalk application"
  default     = "my-application"
}

variable "environment_version_label" {
  description = "Version label for the Elastic Beanstalk environment"
  default     = "v1"
}

variable "solution_stack_name" {
  description = "Solution stack name for the Elastic Beanstalk environment"
  default     = "64bit Amazon Linux 2 v3.3.1 running Python 3.8"
}

variable "cname_prefix" {
  description = "CNAME prefix for the Elastic Beanstalk environment"
  default     = "myapp"
}

variable "domain_name" {
  description = "Domain name for the Route53 hosted zone"
  default     = "example.com"
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_application" "my_application" {
  name        = var.application_name
  description = "My Elastic Beanstalk Application"
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment" "blue_environment" {
  name                = "blue"
  application         = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.my_application.name
  solution_stack_name = var.solution_stack_name
  version_label       = var.environment_version_label
  cname_prefix        = var.cname_prefix
}

resource "aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment" "green_environment" {
  name                = "green"
  application         = aws_elastic_beanstalk_application.my_application.name
  solution_stack_name = var.solution_stack_name
  version_label       = var.environment_version_label
  cname_prefix        = var.cname_prefix
}

resource "aws_route53_hosted_zone" "example_com_zone" {
  name          = var.domain_name
  caller_reference = "my-dns-zone"
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "weighted_blue_record" {
  name    = var.domain_name
  type    = "A"
  zone_id = aws_route53_hosted_zone.example_com_zone.zone_id
  ttl     = 300

  weighted_routing_policy {
    weight = 50
  }

  records = [aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment.blue_environment.endpoint_url]
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "weighted_green_record" {
  name    = var.domain_name
  type    = "A"
  zone_id = aws_route53_hosted_zone.example_com_zone.zone_id
  ttl     = 300

  weighted_routing_policy {
    weight = 50
  }

  records = [aws_elastic_beanstalk_environment.green_environment.endpoint_url]
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **Variables**: Several variables are defined to make the configuration flexible and reusable.
3. **Elastic Beanstalk Application**: An Elastic Beanstalk application is created.
4. **Elastic Beanstalk Environments**: Two environments, "blue" and "green", are created under the same application.
5. **Route53 Hosted Zone**: A Route53 hosted zone is created for the domain `example.com`.
6. **Route53 Records**: Weighted routing records are created for both environments, distributing traffic equally between them.

This setup allows for seamless Blue/Green deployments by managing traffic distribution through Route53.

