### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS Kendra data source with URL exclusion and inclusion patterns. It includes the necessary IAM role and Kendra index resources. The Kendra data source is configured to crawl a website using the provided URL patterns.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "kendra_role" {
  name = "kendra-data-source-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "kendra.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_kendra_index" "kendra_index" {
  name       = "kendra-index"
  role_arn   = aws_iam_role.kendra_role.arn
  edition    = "ENTERPRISE_EDITION"
}

resource "aws_kendra_data_source" "kendra_data_source" {
  depends_on = [
    aws_iam_role.kendra_role,
    aws_kendra_index.kendra_index
  ]

  index_id = aws_kendra_index.kendra_index.id
  name     = "kendra-web-crawler"
  type     = "WEBCRAWLER"
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.kendra_role.arn

  configuration {
    web_crawler_configuration {
      url_exclusion_patterns = ["http://example.com/exclude/*"]
      url_inclusion_patterns = ["http://example.com/include/*"]

      urls {
        seed_url_configuration {
          seed_urls = ["http://example.com"]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `kendra-data-source-role` is created with a trust policy allowing Kendra to assume the role.
3. **Kendra Index**: A Kendra index named `kendra-index` is created, associated with the IAM role.
4. **Kendra Data Source**: A Kendra data source named `kendra-web-crawler` is created, configured to crawl a website. The data source uses the IAM role and specifies URL exclusion and inclusion patterns.

