### Description
This Terraform program creates an Amazon Kendra index with user group resolution configured using AWS Single Sign-On (AWS SSO). It includes the necessary IAM role with the appropriate permissions for Kendra operations.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "kendra_index_role" {
  name = "kendra-index-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "kendra.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })

  managed_policy_arns = [
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonKendraFullAccess"
  ]
}

resource "aws_kendra_index" "basic_kendra_index" {
  name       = "basic-kendra-index"
  role_arn   = aws_iam_role.kendra_index_role.arn

  user_group_resolution_configuration {
    user_group_resolution_mode = "AWS_SSO"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a specific region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to your preferred region.
2. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `kendra-index-role` is created with an assume role policy that allows Kendra to assume the role. The role is also attached to the `AmazonKendraFullAccess` managed policy.
3. **Kendra Index**: A Kendra index named `basic-kendra-index` is created, with the IAM role ARN passed to it. The `user_group_resolution_configuration` block specifies the `user_group_resolution_mode` as `AWS_SSO`.

This configuration ensures that the Kendra index is properly set up with user group resolution using AWS SSO, leveraging the necessary IAM role and permissions.

