LLM Output #0:
### Description

This Terraform program creates an AWS Lambda function that runs a JavaScript file named `lambda.js`. It includes the necessary IAM roles and policies to allow the Lambda function to execute. The program also archives the `lambda.js` file into a ZIP archive, which is then used as the code for the Lambda function.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify the desired AWS region
}

# IAM Policy Document for assuming the Lambda execution role
data "aws_iam_policy_document" "assume_role_policy" {
  statement {
    effect = "Allow"
    principals {
      type        = "Service"
      identifiers = ["lambda.amazonaws.com"]
    }
    actions = ["sts:AssumeRole"]
  }
}

# IAM Role for the Lambda function
resource "aws_iam_role" "iam_for_lambda" {
  name               = "iam_for_lambda"
  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.assume_role_policy.json
}

# Attach basic execution policy to the Lambda role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "attach_lambda_basic_execution" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole"
  role       = aws_iam_role.iam_for_lambda.name
}

# Archive the Lambda function code
resource "archive_file" "lambda_archive" {
  type        = "zip"
  source_file = "lambda.js"
  output_path = "lambda_function_payload.zip"
}

# AWS Lambda function
resource "aws_lambda_function" "test_lambda" {
  filename         = archive_file.lambda_archive.output_path
  function_name    = "lambda_function_name"
  role             = aws_iam_role.iam_for_lambda.arn
  handler          = "index.handler"  # Adjust the handler according to your lambda.js file
  runtime          = "nodejs18.x"
  source_code_hash = archive_file.lambda_archive.output_base64sha256
}
```

### Notes

- Ensure that the `lambda.js` file is in the current working directory or provide the correct path in the `source_file` attribute of the `archive_file` resource.
- Adjust the `handler` attribute in the `aws_lambda_function` resource according to the entry point of your `lambda.js` file.
- The `runtime` attribute is set to `nodejs18.x`, but you should adjust it to match the Node.js version you are using.

