### Description
The Terraform program defined below creates a DynamoDB table named "ExampleTableName" and enables contributor insights on it. The program includes the necessary provider configuration and ensures that the contributor insights resource depends on the existence of the DynamoDB table.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify the desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "example_table" {
  name           = "ExampleTableName"
  billing_mode   = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"

  attribute {
    name = "id"
    type = "S"
  }

  key_schema {
    attribute_name = "id"
    key_type       = "HASH"
  }
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_contributor_insights" "example_table_contributor_insights" {
  table_name = aws_dynamodb_table.example_table.name
}
```

This Terraform configuration will create a DynamoDB table with a single attribute "id" of type string and enable contributor insights on that table. The `aws_dynamodb_contributor_insights` resource depends on the `aws_dynamodb_table` resource to ensure that the table exists before enabling contributor insights.

