### Description
This Terraform program creates a serverless Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (MSK) cluster with 3 broker nodes. The configuration includes the necessary provider setup, IAM roles, and the MSK cluster resource. The MSK cluster is configured with basic settings such as the cluster name, Kafka version, and broker node group information.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

variable "cluster_name" {
  description = "The name of the MSK cluster"
  default     = "my-msk-cluster"
}

variable "kafka_version" {
  description = "The version of Kafka to use"
  default     = "2.8.1"
}

variable "instance_type" {
  description = "The instance type for the broker nodes"
  default     = "kafka.m5.large"
}

variable "client_subnets" {
  description = "List of subnets for the broker nodes"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0fedcba9876543210"]
}

variable "security_groups" {
  description = "List of security groups for the broker nodes"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "msk_role" {
  name = "${var.cluster_name}-msk-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "ec2.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "msk_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonMSKFullAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.msk_role.name
}

resource "aws_msk_cluster" "msk_cluster" {
  cluster_name           = var.cluster_name
  kafka_version          = var.kafka_version
  number_of_broker_nodes = 3

  broker_node_group_info {
    client_subnets = var.client_subnets
    instance_type  = var.instance_type
    security_groups = var.security_groups
  }

  depends_on = [aws_iam_role_policy_attachment.msk_policy]
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with the region `us-west-2`.
2. **Variables**: Several variables are defined with default values to customize the MSK cluster configuration.
3. **IAM Role**: An IAM role is created for the MSK cluster with a trust policy allowing EC2 to assume the role.
4. **IAM Role Policy Attachment**: The `AmazonMSKFullAccess` policy is attached to the IAM role to grant necessary permissions.
5. **MSK Cluster**: The MSK cluster is created with the specified number of broker nodes, Kafka version, and broker node group information. The cluster depends on the IAM role policy attachment to ensure the role has the necessary permissions before the cluster is created.

