### Description of the Terraform Program

This Terraform program sets up the infrastructure for a video streaming site using AWS CloudFront and AWS S3. It includes the following components:

1. **AWS S3 Bucket**: This bucket will store the video content that needs to be distributed globally.
2. **AWS CloudFront Distribution**: This distribution will serve the video content from the S3 bucket using a global CDN network, ensuring fast and reliable delivery to users worldwide.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "video_content_bucket" {
  bucket = "video-content-bucket-${random_string.bucket_suffix.result}"
  acl    = "private"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "cloudfront.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = "s3:GetObject"
        Resource = "${aws_s3_bucket.video_content_bucket.arn}/*"
        Condition = {
          StringEquals = {
            "AWS:SourceArn" = aws_cloudfront_distribution.video_streaming_distribution.arn
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  })

  tags = {
    Name        = "VideoContentBucket"
    Environment = "Production"
  }
}

resource "random_string" "bucket_suffix" {
  length  = 8
  special = false
}

resource "aws_cloudfront_distribution" "video_streaming_distribution" {
  origin {
    domain_name = aws_s3_bucket.video_content_bucket.bucket_regional_domain_name
    origin_id   = "myS3Origin"

    s3_origin_config {
      origin_access_identity = aws_cloudfront_origin_access_identity.origin_access_identity.cloudfront_access_identity_path
    }
  }

  enabled             = true
  is_ipv6_enabled     = true
  comment             = "Video Streaming Distribution"
  default_root_object = "index.html"

  default_cache_behavior {
    allowed_methods  = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    cached_methods   = ["GET", "HEAD"]
    target_origin_id = "myS3Origin"

    forwarded_values {
      query_string = false
      cookies {
        forward = "none"
      }
    }

    viewer_protocol_policy = "redirect-to-https"
  }

  restrictions {
    geo_restriction {
      restriction_type = "none"
    }
  }

  viewer_certificate {
    cloudfront_default_certificate = true
  }

  tags = {
    Name        = "VideoStreamingDistribution"
    Environment = "Production"
  }
}

resource "aws_cloudfront_origin_access_identity" "origin_access_identity" {
  comment = "OAI for Video Content Bucket"
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-east-1` region.
2. **S3 Bucket**: An S3 bucket named `video-content-bucket-<random_suffix>` is created. The bucket policy allows CloudFront to access the objects stored in the bucket.
3. **Random String**: A random string is generated to ensure the bucket name is unique.
4. **CloudFront Distribution**: A CloudFront distribution is set up to serve content from the S3 bucket. It includes configurations for caching, viewer protocols, and restrictions.
5. **Origin Access Identity**: An origin access identity (OAI) is created to allow CloudFront to access the S3 bucket securely.

This setup ensures that the video content is globally distributed efficiently using AWS CloudFront and stored securely in an S3 bucket.

