LLM Output #0:
### Description of the Terraform Program

This Terraform program sets up a PostgreSQL 15 instance on AWS RDS within specific public subnets for running Airbyte connector test cases. The instance uses managed settings for low maintenance, with an allocated storage of 5 GB and an instance type of "db.t3.micro". The program includes the necessary provider configuration and IAM roles.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "vpc_id" {
  description = "The ID of the VPC where the RDS instance will be deployed"
  default     = "vpc-12345678"  # Replace with your VPC ID
}

variable "subnet_ids" {
  description = "List of subnet IDs where the RDS instance will be deployed"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = ["subnet-abcdef12", "subnet-34567890"]  # Replace with your subnet IDs
}

resource "aws_db_subnet_group" "airbyte_subnet_group" {
  name       = "airbyte-subnet-group"
  subnet_ids = var.subnet_ids
  tags = {
    Name = "Airbyte Subnet Group"
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "airbyte_rds_role" {
  name = "airbyte-rds-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "rds.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "airbyte_rds_policy" {
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AmazonRDSFullAccess"
  role       = aws_iam_role.airbyte_rds_role.name
}

resource "aws_db_instance" "airbyte_postgres_instance" {
  allocated_storage    = 5
  engine               = "postgres"
  engine_version       = "15"
  instance_class       = "db.t3.micro"
  db_name              = "airbyte_db"
  username             = "airbyte_user"
  password             = "securepassword123"
  db_subnet_group_name = aws_db_subnet_group.airbyte_subnet_group.name
  vpc_security_group_ids = ["sg-12345678"]  # Replace with your security group ID
  skip_final_snapshot  = true
  iam_database_authentication_enabled = true
  iam_roles            = [aws_iam_role.airbyte_rds_role.arn]

  tags = {
    Name = "Airbyte PostgreSQL Instance"
  }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with a specific region (`us-west-2`). You can change this to your desired region.

2. **Variables**: Two variables are defined for the VPC ID and subnet IDs. Default values are provided for offline validation.

3. **DB Subnet Group**: An `aws_db_subnet_group` resource is created to specify the subnets where the RDS instance will be deployed.

4. **IAM Role and Policy Attachment**: An IAM role (`airbyte_rds_role`) is created with a trust policy allowing RDS to assume the role. The role is attached to the `AmazonRDSFullAccess` policy.

5. **RDS Instance**: An `aws_db_instance` resource is created with the specified parameters:
   - `allocated_storage`: 5 GB
   - `engine`: PostgreSQL
   - `engine_version`: 15
   - `instance_class`: `db.t3.micro`
   - `db_name`: `airbyte_db`
   - `username`: `airbyte_user`
   - `password`: `securepassword123` (replace with a secure password)
   - `db_subnet_group_name`: The name of the created subnet group
   - `vpc_security_group_ids`: Security group ID (replace with your security group ID)
   - `skip_final_snapshot`: Set to `true` to avoid creating a final snapshot when the instance is deleted
   - `iam_database_authentication_enabled`: Enabled for IAM database authentication
   - `iam_roles`: The ARN of the created IAM role

This configuration ensures that the PostgreSQL instance is set up with the required settings and dependencies for running Airbyte connector test cases.

