### Description
This Terraform program creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) that forwards traffic to one or more EC2 instances in a target group. The ALB is configured with a listener that routes incoming HTTP traffic to the target group. The target group is associated with the ALB, and instances can be registered to this target group to receive traffic.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
}

resource "aws_subnet" "public" {
  count             = 2
  vpc_id            = aws_vpc.main.id
  cidr_block        = cidrsubnet(aws_vpc.main.cidr_block, 8, count.index)
  availability_zone = element(data.aws_availability_zones.available.names, count.index)
}

data "aws_availability_zones" "available" {}

resource "aws_security_group" "lb_sg" {
  name        = "lb-sg"
  description = "Security group for the load balancer"
  vpc_id      = aws_vpc.main.id

  ingress {
    from_port   = 80
    to_port     = 80
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }

  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}

resource "aws_lb" "my_application_load_balancer" {
  name               = "my-application-load-balancer"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  security_groups    = [aws_security_group.lb_sg.id]
  subnets            = aws_subnet.public[*].id

  access_logs {
    bucket = "my-alb-logs-bucket"
    prefix = "alb-logs/"
    enabled = true
  }

  enable_deletion_protection = true
}

resource "aws_lb_target_group" "my_target_group" {
  name     = "my-target-group"
  port     = 80
  protocol = "HTTP"
  vpc_id   = aws_vpc.main.id
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "my_listener" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.my_application_load_balancer.arn
  port              = 80
  protocol          = "HTTP"

  default_action {
    type             = "forward"
    target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.my_target_group.arn
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **VPC and Subnets**: A VPC and two public subnets are created within the VPC.
3. **Security Group**: A security group is created to allow HTTP traffic on port 80.
4. **Load Balancer**: An Application Load Balancer is created with the specified security group and subnets. Access logs are enabled and stored in an S3 bucket named `my-alb-logs-bucket`.
5. **Target Group**: A target group is created to manage the instances that will receive traffic from the load balancer.
6. **Listener**: A listener is created to route incoming HTTP traffic to the target group.

This configuration ensures that the load balancer, target group, and listener are correctly set up to forward traffic to the specified instances.

