### Description
This Terraform program creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with a fixed-response action. The ALB is configured with a listener and a listener rule that returns a fixed response. Additionally, a target group and its attachment are defined, although they are not directly used in the fixed-response action.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "my_load_balancer" {
  name               = "my-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  security_groups    = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]
  subnets            = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0123456789abcdef1"]

  access_logs {
    bucket = "my-alb-logs"
    prefix = "logs/"
    enabled = true
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "my_listener" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.my_load_balancer.arn
  port              = "80"
  protocol          = "HTTP"

  default_action {
    type = "fixed-response"

    fixed_response {
      content_type = "text/plain"
      message_body = "Fixed Response"
      status_code  = "200"
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_listener_rule" "my_listener_rule" {
  listener_arn = aws_lb_listener.my_listener.arn
  priority     = 1

  action {
    type = "fixed-response"

    fixed_response {
      content_type = "text/plain"
      message_body = "Fixed Response Rule"
      status_code  = "200"
    }
  }

  condition {
    field  = "http-header"
    values = ["User-Agent", "curl"]
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_target_group" "my_target_group" {
  name     = "my-target-group"
  port     = 80
  protocol = "HTTP"
  vpc_id   = "vpc-0123456789abcdef0"
}

resource "aws_lb_target_group_attachment" "my_target_group_attachment" {
  target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.my_target_group.arn
  target_id        = "i-0123456789abcdef0"
  port             = 80
}
```

### Explanation
- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
- **Load Balancer (`aws_lb`)**: An Application Load Balancer is created with specified subnets and security groups. Access logs are enabled and stored in an S3 bucket.
- **Listener (`aws_lb_listener`)**: A listener is attached to the load balancer on port 80 using the HTTP protocol. It has a default action that returns a fixed response.
- **Listener Rule (`aws_lb_listener_rule`)**: A listener rule is defined with a higher priority that also returns a fixed response. The rule is triggered when the `User-Agent` header contains "curl".
- **Target Group (`aws_lb_target_group`)**: A target group is defined, though it is not directly used in the fixed-response action.
- **Target Group Attachment (`aws_lb_target_group_attachment`)**: An EC2 instance is attached to the target group, though it is not directly used in the fixed-response action.

This configuration ensures that the load balancer is set up with a fixed-response action, and all dependencies are correctly managed.

